  - id: "project:project-tin-audit-checker:overview"
    category: project
    question: What is Montasim's TIN Audit Checker - Bangladesh project?
    text: "Montasim built TIN Audit Checker - Bangladesh, a dataset project. A private, browser-only lookup for checking whether a Bangladesh TIN appears on a historical NBR risk-based audit selection list for AY 2023-24, covering 72,342 returns. His role covered data modeling, privacy design, and release engineering, with scope spanning client-side lookup, data provenance, and public distribution. Users can search the historical list quickly, including on mobile. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-tin-audit-checker","case-study:tin-audit-checker:problem","case-study:tin-audit-checker:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "A private, browser-only lookup for checking whether a Bangladesh TIN appears on a historical NBR risk-based audit selection list for AY 2023-24, covering 72,342 returns.\n\nfalse\n2026-04-30T09:35:36Z\n7d915fdb881c99faea75b5ce829d15dce17359ba\n2026-04-30T11:59:39Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/tin-audit-checker\nproject-tin-audit-checker\nassets/projects/tin-audit-checker.png\nhttps://tin-audit-checker.netlify.app\nhttps://tin-audit-checker.netlify.app/favicon.ico?favicon.0x3dzn~oxb6tn.ico\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nTailwind","A list circulated as the NBR Risk-Based Audit selection for assessment year 2023-24, covering 72,342 returns, and searching it manually for one TIN is slow, especially on a phone. The obvious fix, a server-side search API, would send every person's tax identifier to another application server and its logs.\nThe data is a historical list, not a live audit or compliance status.\nThe claimed NBR provenance, accuracy, completeness, and redistribution rights have not been established.\nBecause the dataset ships to the","Users can search the historical list quickly, including on mobile.\nTyped TINs are never submitted to an application API.\nA match returns only the bounded details mapped from the list.\nBoth matches and non-matches tell the user to confirm their status with current official sources."
  - id: "project:project-tin-audit-checker:technology"
    category: project
    question: Which technologies did Montasim use for TIN Audit Checker - Bangladesh?
    text: "Montasim built TIN Audit Checker - Bangladesh with Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, JSON, SheetJS. The product goal is clear: A private, browser-only lookup for checking whether a Bangladesh TIN appears on a historical NBR risk-based audit selection list for AY 2023-24, covering 72,342 returns. More importantly, the architecture is explicit: A Next.js page fetches the static JSON dataset once per session and caches it in memory. Each search normalizes the input and runs an exact match in the browser, and there is no API that receives a TIN. That gives technical reviewers a concrete system boundary to discuss instead of a list of framework keywords."
