  - id: "project:project-content-types-lite:overview"
    category: project
    question: What is Montasim's content-types-lite project?
    text: "Montasim built content-types-lite, a package project. Tiny, type-safe HTTP media type constants and utilities for parsing, formatting, matching, and validation. His role covered library design and package engineering, with scope spanning typed APIs, compatibility, and package distribution. Consumers can parse and serialize Content-Type values. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-content-types-lite","case-study:content-types-lite:problem","case-study:content-types-lite:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "Tiny, type-safe HTTP media type constants and utilities for parsing, formatting, matching, and validation.\n\nfalse\n2025-01-29T13:00:26Z\n78eeb6ca02149b23e1486078e8b02ac009faf0b5\n2025-01-29T11:05:22Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/content-types-lite\nproject-content-types-lite\nassets/projects/content-types-lite.png\nhttps://content-types-lite.netlify.app\nhttps://content-types-lite.netlify.app/favicon.svg\nhttps://www.npmjs.com/package/content-types-lite\nTypeScript\nESM\nCommonJS\ntsup\nTanStack Start\nReact\nTailwind","Applications keep reimplementing Content-Type parsing and negotiation, and each version handles edge cases slightly differently. The usual alternative is importing a larger dependency tree for what is a focused HTTP-header task.\nQuoted parameters and malformed header values must parse predictably.\nThe package output must work for both ESM and CommonJS consumers.\nThe public API must stay small and type-safe with no runtime dependencies.","Consumers can parse and serialize Content-Type values.\nConsumers can validate and compare media types.\nThe package works from both ESM and CommonJS.\nDevelopers can test behavior interactively in the documentation app."
  - id: "project:project-content-types-lite:technology"
    category: project
    question: Which technologies did Montasim use for content-types-lite?
    text: "Montasim built content-types-lite with TypeScript, ESM, CommonJS, tsup, TanStack Start, React, Tailwind CSS, Vite, Vitest, Netlify, GitHub Actions, CI/CD. The product goal is clear: Tiny, type-safe HTTP media type constants and utilities for parsing, formatting, matching, and validation. More importantly, the architecture is explicit: The core is a pure TypeScript library with its own tests, built into dual ESM and CommonJS outputs with typed exports. A React documentation and playground app in the same workspace consumes the local package, so the docs always run the current code. That gives technical reviewers a concrete system boundary to discuss instead of a list of framework keywords."
