  - id: "project:project-client-parser:overview"
    category: project
    question: What is Montasim's client-parser project?
    text: "Montasim built client-parser, a package project. A tiny, type-safe client classifier with User-Agent, Client Hints, and HTTP header support. His role covered library design and package engineering, with scope spanning typed APIs, compatibility, and package distribution. Consumers can classify common client strings. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-client-parser","case-study:client-parser:problem","case-study:client-parser:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "A tiny, type-safe client classifier with User-Agent, Client Hints, and HTTP header support.\n\nfalse\n2025-07-21T15:00:55Z\ndbfdfced68ab10a02d2de8c4a21d0fd3cf6be2b3\n2025-07-21T15:01:25Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/client-parser\nproject-client-parser\nassets/projects/client-parser.png\nhttps://client-parser.netlify.app\nhttps://client-parser.netlify.app/favicon.svg\nhttps://www.npmjs.com/package/client-parser\nTypeScript\nESM\nCommonJS\ntsup\nTanStack Start\nReact\nTailwind CSS\nVite\nVitest\nNetlify\nGitHub","Analytics and diagnostics need a normalized view of which browser, OS, device, or bot made a request. The raw User-Agent string can be changed by any client, and many parsers are heavy or quietly encourage using the result for decisions it cannot support.\nUser-Agent classification is heuristic, and any client can spoof it.\nClient Hints availability varies and may be restricted for privacy.\nResults cannot safely drive authentication, authorization, or capability decisions.","Consumers can classify common client strings.\nResults are enriched with Client Hints when they are available.\nAnalytics and presentation code can distinguish bots, devices, and browsers.\nDevelopers can inspect parsing behavior in the playground without sending their input anywhere."
