    text: "Montasim built client-parser with TypeScript, ESM, CommonJS, tsup, TanStack Start, React, Tailwind CSS, Vite, Vitest, Netlify, GitHub Actions, CI/CD. The product goal is clear: A tiny, type-safe client classifier with User-Agent, Client Hints, and HTTP header support. More importantly, the architecture is explicit: Pure parsing and normalization rules produce a typed result model, packaged with zero dependencies in both ESM and CommonJS. A workspace-linked playground and documentation app runs the library locally, and a regression corpus guards the rules as clients change. That gives technical reviewers a concrete system boundary to discuss instead of a list of framework keywords."
