    supportingExcerpts[3]: "A deployment-readiness skill for Codex and Claude Code that detects framework and runtime behavior, validates Netlify configuration and output paths, and prepares evidence-backed local repairs without implicitly","A build can succeed locally and still fail on Netlify, or deploy and serve the wrong thing, because the base path, publish directory, runtime model, redirects, adapter, or environment requirements were misidentified. These are not compiler errors, so they tend to surface only after a deploy, as a site that opens empty or where only the home page works.\nStatic, SPA, hybrid, and SSR apps each need a different routing and function contract.\nNetlify adapter behavior depends on the framework and its version.\nDashboard","Agents can classify a project's runtime model before touching its configuration.\nAgents make minimal local configuration repairs instead of rewriting netlify.toml.\nRoot and nested routes and the output shape are verified locally.\nReports separate a deployment-ready local state from dashboard and deploy actions that were not performed."
