    question: What is Montasim's find-ui-inconsistencies project?
    text: "Montasim built find-ui-inconsistencies, a skill project. A frontend-review skill for Codex and Claude Code that evaluates typography, spacing, color, layout, shared UI, responsive behavior, skeletons, motion, and visible accessibility states while preserving intentional design direction. His role covered agent workflow design and automation engineering, with scope spanning agent workflow, validation automation, and packaging. Agents can produce UI findings that someone else can reproduce. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-find-ui-inconsistencies","case-study:find-ui-inconsistencies:problem","case-study:find-ui-inconsistencies:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "A frontend-review skill for Codex and Claude Code that evaluates typography, spacing, color, layout, shared UI, responsive behavior, skeletons, motion, and visible accessibility states while preserving intentional design","Visual inconsistencies are often reported from a single screenshot, with no record of the route, build, or state it came from and nothing to compare it against. Without responsive states or a systemic root cause, a fix tends to patch one page while the underlying drift stays in place.\nA screenshot only counts as evidence when it is tied to a route, viewport, time or build, and state.\nResponsive and accessibility behavior can only be judged across multiple widths and interaction states.\nA request for an audit does","Agents can produce UI findings that someone else can reproduce.\nFindings distinguish observed defects from inferred causes.\nAgents propose the smallest systemic fix rather than page-level patches.\nWhen implementation is requested, agents recheck affected viewports, states, motion, focus, tests, and builds."
