    question: What is Montasim's fix-project-metadata-mismatches project?
    text: "Montasim built fix-project-metadata-mismatches, a skill project. An evidence-first maintenance skill for Codex and Claude Code that detects metadata drift across manifests, lockfiles, documentation, deployment configuration, and catalogs, then aligns local files only when requested. His role covered agent workflow design and automation engineering, with scope spanning agent workflow, validation automation, and packaging. Agents can identify conflicting names, versions, and URLs across a project. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-fix-project-metadata-mismatches","case-study:fix-project-metadata-mismatches:problem","case-study:fix-project-metadata-mismatches:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "An evidence-first maintenance skill for Codex and Claude Code that detects metadata drift across manifests, lockfiles, documentation, deployment configuration, and catalogs, then aligns local files only when","A project's name, version, links, and compatibility claims are repeated across manifests, lockfiles, documentation, deployment configuration, and catalogs, and those copies drift apart. Users then follow broken links, run the wrong install command, or read conflicting compatibility claims. Finding and reconciling every copy by hand is slow and easy to get wrong.\nEach metadata field has its own authoritative source, so no single file can be treated as the truth for everything.\nA human-facing description must match","Agents can identify conflicting names, versions, and URLs across a project.\nAgents repair only the local copies they are authorized to change.\nUnknown values are preserved for manual resolution instead of being overwritten.\nRemaining remote actions are reported separately from completed local work."
