    factIds[3]: "project:project-update-skillfolio-catalog","case-study:update-skillfolio-catalog:problem","case-study:update-skillfolio-catalog:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "A catalog-maintenance skill that resolves public package and repository evidence, updates the correct local authorities, regenerates derived data, and verifies the target Skillfolio application without implicitly deploying","Adding a skill to a catalog touches several consumers that duplicate its data, such as README indexes and the sitemap. It can also import stale package or repository facts, or treat a request to \"publish\" as permission to deploy. Either mistake breaks the catalog or makes an external change nobody approved.\nCatalog schemas and the consumers that read them vary between target apps.\nRepository, package, version, and compatibility facts must be verified against primary sources.\nEditing the local catalog does not","Agents can resolve a canonical skill identity before editing the catalog.\nAgents add or update a single valid entry.\nREADME indexes and the sitemap stay aligned with the catalog.\nReports describe local completion without implying that anything was published."
