    supportingExcerpts[3]: "An evidence-based skill for Codex and Claude Code that validates crawler-visible Open Graph and Twitter Card metadata, repairs framework-native metadata, and creates branded 1200×630 preview assets when","A page can look correct in the browser while link-preview crawlers see missing or client-only metadata, an image that is too small or unreachable, or an old card the platform has cached. Implementation problems and cache problems need different fixes, and confusing them leads teams to rewrite correct metadata or wait on a cache that will never refresh.\nSocial platforms select and cache cards with proprietary rules that cannot be simulated or controlled.\nMetadata must be visible to crawlers in the server HTML, and","Agents can tell a missing card apart from a cached one.\nIncomplete, relative, or client-only metadata is repaired at its source.\nA branded large-image asset is created only when one is needed.\nAgents verify the local implementation and deployed crawler eligibility without promising a platform-specific layout."
