    supportingExcerpts[3]: "A SupportKori-specific frontend skill that integrates one theme-consistent support trigger across websites and browser extensions, checking lifecycle, CSP and runtime","A support widget can load without errors and still clash with a site's design, mount more than once, violate the Content Security Policy, or fail inside a browser extension. Because the widget is part of the product interface, each of these problems reaches users directly.\nIntegration must use the repository's established SupportKori contract rather than inventing a generic embed.\nWebsites and extensions have different lifecycle, CSP, permission, and iframe boundaries.\nRemote configuration and publication remain","Agents can audit or integrate SupportKori without replacing an existing valid setup.\nThe widget follows the host's visual and interaction conventions.\nExtension-specific security boundaries stay explicit.\nVerification covers both rendered behavior and integration safety."
