  - id: "project:project-educanvas:overview"
    category: project
    question: What is Montasim's EduCanvas project?
    text: "Montasim built EduCanvas, a template project. A theme-driven education website and content-management starter built with Next.js. His role covered application architecture and full-stack engineering, with scope spanning content architecture, authentication, and deployment. Developers can deploy one starter for three institution categories. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-educanvas","case-study:educanvas:problem","case-study:educanvas:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "A theme-driven education website and content-management starter built with Next.js.\n\nfalse\n2026-07-27T17:41:53Z\nf0ea922b85f28025d1e3bf81d5a9b4ff413cda56\n2026-07-27T17:50:31Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/EduCanvas\nproject-educanvas\nassets/projects/educanvas.png\n\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nTailwind CSS\nMongoDB\nBetter Auth\nGoogle Drive API\nResend\nREST APIs\nRadix UI\nPlaywright\nSystem Design\nEduCanvas\ncontent-management\neducation\nnextjs\ntailwindcss\ntypescript\nwebsite-starter\ntemplate","Education organizations need familiar public information pages and publishing workflows. Cloning a whole codebase for each institution creates drift between the copies and makes every fix costly to maintain.\nThree institution types and multiple layouts must share behavior without leaking content or theme between them.\nMongoDB, Google OAuth and Drive, and Resend are optional services that each deployment has to configure.\nPublic pages must stay usable on read-only defaults when database-backed administration is","Developers can deploy one starter for three institution categories.\nAdministrators can publish content and manage enquiries.\nVisitors see the configured branding and layout on shared routes.\nDeployments can fall back to read-only repository defaults where documented."
  - id: "project:project-educanvas:technology"
    category: project
    question: Which technologies did Montasim use for EduCanvas?
    text: "Montasim built EduCanvas with Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, MongoDB, Better Auth, Google Drive API, Resend, REST APIs, Radix UI, Playwright, System Design. The product goal is clear: A theme-driven education website and content-management starter built with Next.js. More importantly, the architecture is explicit: Next.js serves both public and admin routes, which call feature-owned modules for content, admissions, and media. Institution and visual-theme settings are centralized as configuration and tokens, and MongoDB, authentication, Drive, and email sit behind adapters with an enforced server boundary. That gives technical reviewers a concrete system boundary to discuss instead of a list of framework keywords."
