    question: What is Montasim's Project Management project?
    text: "Montasim built Project Management, a website project. A collaborative project-management application with React dashboards for tasks, subtasks, bugs, discussions, members, and project progress. Montasim contributed frontend development and responsive Tailwind CSS interfaces. His role covered frontend developer on a collaborative project, with scope spanning react interface development and responsive Tailwind CSS presentation for project and team workflows. The repository presents project overview, task, bug, discussion, and member-management interfaces. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-project-management","case-study:project-management:problem","case-study:project-management:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "true\nA collaborative project-management application with React dashboards for tasks, subtasks, bugs, discussions, members, and project progress. Montasim contributed frontend development and responsive Tailwind CSS interfaces.\nfalse\n2020-10-01T04:35:09Z\n77d8ead1a20cc7d2156d53673758efe0ef4c0abf\n2020-09-19T04:26:11Z\nfalse\nhttps://github.com/mdjahidhasan009/Project_Management\nproject-project-management\nnull\nJavaScript\nReact\nRedux\nTailwind CSS\nNode.js\nExpress.js\nMongoDB\nMongoose\nProject","Software teams need to review tasks, bugs, discussions, and membership in one project context. The frontend must organize these related workflows without forcing users to reconstruct project status across unrelated screens.\nThe README explicitly identifies Montasim as the frontend developer, so backend capabilities are application context rather than a claim of personal backend ownership.\nThe repository includes legacy React and backend dependencies, and no current live deployment or end-to-end execution was","The repository presents project overview, task, bug, discussion, and member-management interfaces.\nFrontend source connects project controls to Redux actions and API request handling.\nThe project provides evidence of collaborative frontend work without asserting deployment availability or measured productivity improvements."
  - id: "project:project-project-management:technology"
    category: project
    question: Which technologies did Montasim use for Project Management?
    text: "Montasim built Project Management with JavaScript, React, Redux, Tailwind CSS, Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB, Mongoose. The product goal is clear: A collaborative project-management application with React dashboards for tasks, subtasks, bugs, discussions, members, and project progress. Montasim contributed frontend development and responsive Tailwind CSS interfaces. More importantly, the architecture is explicit: React routes and Redux state connect project interfaces to an Express API. The repository also contains Mongoose project models and controllers for tasks, subtasks, bugs, discussions, and membership. That gives technical reviewers a concrete system boundary to discuss instead of a list of framework keywords."
