  - id: "case-study:make-app-netlify-ready:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the make-app-netlify-ready case study?
    text: "A build can succeed locally and still fail on Netlify, or deploy and serve the wrong thing, because the base path, publish directory, runtime model, redirects, adapter, or environment requirements were misidentified. These are not compiler errors, so they tend to surface only after a deploy, as a site that opens empty or where only the home page works. Montasim owned agent workflow design and automation engineering, covering agent workflow, validation automation, and packaging. The solution also had to respect “Static, SPA, hybrid, and SSR apps each need a different routing and function contract”; “Netlify adapter behavior depends on the framework and its version”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
