  - id: "case-study:make-app-netlify-ready:architecture"
    category: case-study
    question: How did Montasim structure the make-app-netlify-ready solution?
    text: "The skill detects the package manager, framework, and runtime model, then writes down an explicit build contract. A Python auditor checks netlify.toml and the build output against that contract using documented patterns, and local build and route checks confirm the repair before any remote step is handed back for authorization. A representative decision was “Write the build contract before changing configuration”: Recording where the build runs, what it produces, and which directory is published makes most deploy bugs visible in writing first. Configuration changes then stay minimal and traceable. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
