  - id: "case-study:deploy-prebuilt-app-to-netlify:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the deploy-prebuilt-app-to-netlify case study?
    text: "Teams that already have a built application often deploy it through a hosting flow designed for source code. That path can trigger unnecessary rebuilds, publish the wrong directory, or upload unsafe local artifacts such as secrets and caches. Montasim owned agent workflow design and automation engineering, covering deployment, deterministic validation, and portable distribution. The solution also had to respect “The requested artifact must be validated before any remote mutation”; “Secrets, source trees, caches, and unrelated files must never enter the deploy payload”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
