  - id: "case-study:deploy-prebuilt-app-to-netlify:architecture"
    category: case-study
    question: How did Montasim structure the deploy-prebuilt-app-to-netlify solution?
    text: "A local preflight checks the artifact and its publish directory before anything remote happens. The skill then selects the Netlify CLI flow behind explicit mutation gates and finishes by verifying the deployed URL and its content. A representative decision was “Deploy the artifact, not the repository”: Prebuilt delivery stays separate from source builds and their dependency graph, so the build that was validated locally is the one that gets published. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
