  - id: "case-study:make-project-github-ready:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the make-project-github-ready case study?
    text: "A codebase can build and pass tests while its Git identity, metadata, security guidance, community files, secret hygiene, and CI are not ready for public collaboration. Making it public exposes all of that at once, including whatever is buried in the history. The move needs to be a deliberate security and operations change rather than a single click. Montasim owned agent workflow design and automation engineering, covering agent workflow, validation automation, and packaging. The solution also had to respect “Creating a repository, changing visibility, changing branch settings, and pushing are external mutations”; “A license and a homepage URL cannot be assumed or invented”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
