  - id: "case-study:make-project-github-ready:architecture"
    category: case-study
    question: How did Montasim structure the make-project-github-ready solution?
    text: "A local auditor inventories manifests, Git state, community files, and CI workflows, and metadata rules turn that inventory into proposed repository settings. Remote changes go through the GitHub CLI or API only when authorized, and each one is read back to confirm the result. A representative decision was “Separate local readiness from remote mutations”: Preparing files locally is reversible, while creating a repository or changing visibility is not. Keeping the stages apart lets the owner review everything before anything external changes. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
