  - id: "case-study:fix-social-link-previews:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the fix-social-link-previews case study?
    text: "A page can look correct in the browser while link-preview crawlers see missing or client-only metadata, an image that is too small or unreachable, or an old card the platform has cached. Implementation problems and cache problems need different fixes, and confusing them leads teams to rewrite correct metadata or wait on a cache that will never refresh. Montasim owned agent workflow design and automation engineering, covering agent workflow, validation automation, and packaging. The solution also had to respect “Social platforms select and cache cards with proprietary rules that cannot be simulated or controlled”; “Metadata must be visible to crawlers in the server HTML, and image URLs must be reachable remotely”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
