  - id: "case-study:find-ui-inconsistencies:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the find-ui-inconsistencies case study?
    text: "Visual inconsistencies are often reported from a single screenshot, with no record of the route, build, or state it came from and nothing to compare it against. Without responsive states or a systemic root cause, a fix tends to patch one page while the underlying drift stays in place. Montasim owned agent workflow design and automation engineering, covering agent workflow, validation automation, and packaging. The solution also had to respect “A screenshot only counts as evidence when it is tied to a route, viewport, time or build, and state”; “Responsive and accessibility behavior can only be judged across multiple widths and interaction states”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
