    question: What problem did Montasim address in the EduCanvas case study?
    text: "Education organizations need familiar public information pages and publishing workflows. Cloning a whole codebase for each institution creates drift between the copies and makes every fix costly to maintain. Montasim owned application architecture and full-stack engineering, covering content architecture, authentication, and deployment. The solution also had to respect “Three institution types and multiple layouts must share behavior without leaking content or theme between them”; “MongoDB, Google OAuth and Drive, and Resend are optional services that each deployment has to configure”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
