  - id: "case-study:educanvas:architecture"
    category: case-study
    question: How did Montasim structure the EduCanvas solution?
    text: "Next.js serves both public and admin routes, which call feature-owned modules for content, admissions, and media. Institution and visual-theme settings are centralized as configuration and tokens, and MongoDB, authentication, Drive, and email sit behind adapters with an enforced server boundary. A representative decision was “Split identity tokens from layout composition”: Institution branding lives in tokens and page structure lives in layouts, so either can change without touching the other. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
