  - id: "case-study:coaching-management:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the Coaching Management case study?
    text: "Coaching institutes often split student records, class structures, attendance devices, fee collection, expenses, and communication across disconnected tools. Operators need one system without allowing one organization to see or mutate another organization’s data. Montasim owned client platform architecture and full-stack engineering, covering multi-tenant RBAC, academic operations, finance, biometric integration, and messaging infrastructure. The solution also had to respect “Every academic and financial workflow must preserve organization isolation and granular role permissions”; “Students and teachers share physical biometric devices even though they have different domain records and responsibilities”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
