    category: case-study
    question: What did Montasim deliver and achieve with client-parser?
    text: "Montasim implemented browser, OS, device, mobile, and bot classification. He added Client Hints support and normalized typed results. He created representative regression tests and package builds. He built a playground that parses input locally in the page without a server parser. The resulting capabilities and outcomes are “Consumers can classify common client strings”; “Results are enriched with Client Hints when they are available”; “Analytics and presentation code can distinguish bots, devices, and browsers”; “Developers can inspect parsing behavior in the playground without sending their input anywhere”. This gives a reviewer a traceable line from Montasim's implementation work to the product capabilities and limits that followed."
