    question: What problem did Montasim address in the Shrnkly case study?
    text: "People who share links, short-lived text or code, and QR codes usually need a separate tool for each. Those tools give the sharer little control over custom slugs, access, expiry, or basic view and click records, so the same lifecycle questions are answered differently in every place. Montasim owned product design and full-stack engineering, covering product workflows, data boundaries, and delivery. The solution also had to respect “Password protection is application access control, not a safe place to store secrets”; “Logging clicks and views has privacy and data retention implications”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
