    category: case-study
    question: How did Montasim structure the Shrnkly solution?
    text: "A localized Next.js interface handles URL, text, and QR creation, while server actions and routes perform creation, redirects, and access checks. Prisma persists the records to MongoDB, and authentication, validation, and QR and browser-share adapters support those core flows. A representative decision was “Use one access model for links and text shares”: URLs and text shares follow the same persistence and lifecycle rules, so expiry, passwords, and limits behave consistently instead of being reimplemented per content type. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
