  - id: "case-study:content-types-lite:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the content-types-lite case study?
    text: "Applications keep reimplementing Content-Type parsing and negotiation, and each version handles edge cases slightly differently. The usual alternative is importing a larger dependency tree for what is a focused HTTP-header task. Montasim owned library design and package engineering, covering typed APIs, compatibility, and package distribution. The solution also had to respect “Quoted parameters and malformed header values must parse predictably”; “The package output must work for both ESM and CommonJS consumers”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
