  - id: "case-study:content-types-lite:architecture"
    category: case-study
    question: How did Montasim structure the content-types-lite solution?
    text: "The core is a pure TypeScript library with its own tests, built into dual ESM and CommonJS outputs with typed exports. A React documentation and playground app in the same workspace consumes the local package, so the docs always run the current code. A representative decision was “Keep runtime dependencies at zero”: A dependency-free package stays small and easy to audit. The cost is leaving out broad convenience helpers in favor of a focused surface. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
