  - id: "case-study:http-status-lite:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the http-status-lite case study?
    text: "Developers need status-code names, categories, and lifecycle metadata. Without a library they fall back on memorized numeric checks or hand-written lists that go stale, and many alternatives bring a heavier dependency than the task needs. Montasim owned library design and package engineering, covering typed APIs, compatibility, and package distribution. The solution also had to respect “The IANA registry changes over time”; “Obsolete, temporary, and unused codes must remain distinguishable”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
