    question: How did Montasim structure the http-status-lite solution?
    text: "A committed snapshot of the IANA registry generates the typed library. Constants, predicates, and metadata are exposed as separately importable entry points, and a workspace-linked interactive reference plus automated registry and release workflows keep the snapshot and package in step. A representative decision was “Commit the registry snapshot”: Builds read a reviewed file instead of fetching the registry at runtime, which makes them deterministic. The trade-off is periodic maintenance when the registry changes. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
