    question: What did Montasim deliver and achieve with http-status-lite?
    text: "Montasim built the typed registry, lookups, parsers, and status-class predicates. He modeled permanent, temporary, obsolete, and unused entries. He added generator drift checks and package publishing gates. He implemented an interactive status reference that consumes the local library. The resulting capabilities and outcomes are “Consumers can retrieve name, category, and lifecycle metadata for status codes”; “Consumers can classify codes into success, client error, and server error categories”; “Consumers can parse and validate status codes”; “Builds rely on a reviewable standards snapshot without runtime network access”. This gives a reviewer a traceable line from Montasim's implementation work to the product capabilities and limits that followed."
