  - id: "case-study:mime-types-lite:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the mime-types-lite case study?
    text: "Upload, download, and HTTP code needs dependable mappings between filenames or extensions and media types. Carrying a broad MIME database into every bundle for that job adds weight most applications do not need. Montasim owned library design and package engineering, covering typed APIs, compatibility, and package distribution. The solution also had to respect “One extension can have aliases or ambiguous mappings”; “Lookup must normalize case, dots, and paths without implying that file content was inspected”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
