  - id: "case-study:mmh-telemedicine:delivery"
    category: case-study
    question: What did Montasim deliver and achieve with MyMedicalHub Telemedicine?
    text: "Montasim contributed to the migration and ongoing development of the Next.js and TypeScript telemedicine experience. He implemented strength-exercise recording and state support, tenant-feature handling, patient and provider messaging, and guided movement UI behavior. He fixed stale movement media, provider-departure loading, invitation validation, queue updates, and other cross-session lifecycle defects. He worked across WebRTC media hooks, Socket.IO coordination, Redux assessment state, authenticated services, and responsive room components. The resulting capabilities and outcomes are “Patients and providers can coordinate guided movement and exercise sessions through one real-time room experience”; “Exercise changes no longer reuse stale recordings or question state from a previous movement”; “Strength and other tenant-specific workflows can be introduced without forking the telehealth application”; “Departure, connection, and service failures resolve into clearer recovery or redirect paths instead of trapping the session”. This gives a reviewer a traceable line from Montasim's implementation work to the product capabilities and limits that followed."
