    question: How did Montasim structure the Inventory Management System Server solution?
    text: "A single Express entry point applies JSON parsing and CORS, then mounts separate routers for pharmacy and non-pharmacy products, orders, setup, people, returns, and suppliers. Request handlers in the inspected product router call MongoDB collection methods directly. A representative decision was “Organize endpoints by resource”: Dedicated route prefixes keep products apart from people, returns, and supplier records, giving each record type a predictable entry point. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
