    text: "Montasim's opening insight in “I Built a Smaller Content-Type Library by Refusing Feature Creep” is framed as “Why it was needed”: Applications keep reimplementing Content-Type parsing and negotiation, and each version handles edge cases slightly differently. The usual alternative is importing a larger dependency tree for what is a focused HTTP-header task. The useful hiring signal is not the feature itself, but his ability to explain the constraint, trade-off, and engineering judgment behind it in a form another developer can challenge or apply."
