    factIds[2]: "blog:prototyping-a-school-information-architecture","case-study:school-management:problem"
    supportingExcerpts[2]: "Frontend engineering\nfalse\nA school website map branching from home into its resource pages\n/images/blog/school-ia.webp\ncase-study-derived\nproject-school-management\nprototyping-a-school-information-architecture\nPrototyping a School Information Architecture with Next.js\ntools","Students and guardians need familiar routes to notices, routines, results, and admission information. A school-site prototype can explore that navigation and content organization before introducing a live content service.\nPublic pages use repository-local sample content rather than a connected school database.\nAdmin login uses client-side in-memory state and does not establish server-side authentication or authorization.\nThe teacher admin route is a placeholder, and forms should not be assumed to persist"
