    supportingExcerpts[2]: "Web development\nfalse\nReact inventory screens talking to a separate POSDash API through Firebase sign-in\n/images/blog/inventory-client.webp\ncase-study-derived\nproject-warehouse-management-client\nconnecting-inventory-screens-to-a-separate-api\nConnecting Inventory Screens to a Separate API\ntools","An inventory interface has to connect sign-in, item browsing, stock updates, and personal item lists. Each of those screens depends on browser state staying coordinated with a separate API.\nThe client embeds a legacy Heroku API address; current end-to-end operation was not verified.\nOnly some account-oriented routes use the client authentication guard, and backend authorization remains a separate responsibility.\nThis client references warehouse-management-server, not inventory-management-system-server."
