  - id: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer:responsibility"
    category: experience
    question: What did Montasim do as Senior Software Engineer at MyMedicalHub International Ltd.?
    text: "As Senior Software Engineer at MyMedicalHub International Ltd. (Oct 2025 - Present), Montasim lead a team of 3 engineers and own frontend architecture across 3 microservices of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by 1,000+ patients and clinicians. He replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic finite-state-machine engine, so 99.9% of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with 60 FPS MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. He built a Konva.js canvas engine for clinicians to correct range-of-motion measurements, moved MediaRecorder to imperative control to remove lifecycle bugs and memory leaks, led the Redux Toolkit rewrite of the medical-assessment chatbot, and refactored 54+ modules into a presentational/container architecture. He introduced the team code-review process and mentor 3 engineers. For a hiring manager, this is role-specific evidence of what he owned, delivered, or improved at that stage of his career—not a title-only claim."
    factIds[1]: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer"
    supportingExcerpts[1]: "employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nLead a team of **3 engineers** and own frontend architecture across **3 microservices** of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by **1,000+ patients and clinicians**. Replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic **finite-state-machine** engine, so **99.9%** of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with **60 FPS** MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. Built a **Konva.js**"
  - id: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer:stack"
    category: experience
    question: What skills did Montasim apply in his Senior Software Engineer role at MyMedicalHub International Ltd.?
    text: "Montasim applied Next.js, React.js, TypeScript, Redux Toolkit, MediaPipe, WebRTC, Konva.js, Tailwind CSS, Microsoft Azure in this role. Montasim lead a team of 3 engineers and own frontend architecture across 3 microservices of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by 1,000+ patients and clinicians. He replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic finite-state-machine engine, so 99.9% of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with 60 FPS MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. He built a Konva.js canvas engine for clinicians to correct range-of-motion measurements, moved MediaRecorder to imperative control to remove lifecycle bugs and memory leaks, led the Redux Toolkit rewrite of the medical-assessment chatbot, and refactored 54+ modules into a presentational/container architecture. He introduced the team code-review process and mentor 3 engineers. A technical interviewer can therefore discuss the stack through the actual responsibilities and outcomes attached to it, rather than treating each technology as an unsupported proficiency claim."
    factIds[1]: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer"
    supportingExcerpts[1]: "employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nLead a team of **3 engineers** and own frontend architecture across **3 microservices** of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by **1,000+ patients and clinicians**. Replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic **finite-state-machine** engine, so **99.9%** of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with **60 FPS** MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. Built a **Konva.js**"
  - id: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-software-engineer:responsibility"
    category: experience
    question: What did Montasim do as Software Engineer at MyMedicalHub International Ltd.?
    text: "As Software Engineer at MyMedicalHub International Ltd. (Oct 2023 - Sep 2025), Montasim owned the biometric strength-assessment module end to end and led cloud cost and infrastructure work across 4 environments. He cut cloud hosting cost 70% (about $10K a year) by moving from self-managed VMs to Azure App Service with GitHub Actions CI/CD, and improved application performance 40% to Lighthouse 90+ by replacing 5 legacy UI libraries. He designed a feature-flag system and API-driven theming that serve 250+ client configurations from one codebase, and shipped HIPAA-compliant SSO, an automated clinical reporting engine and a session-recording pipeline to AWS S3. He named Employee of the Month in October 2023. For a hiring manager, this is role-specific evidence of what he owned, delivered, or improved at that stage of his career—not a title-only claim."
    factIds[1]: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-software-engineer"
