  - id: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-junior-software-engineer:responsibility"
    category: experience
    question: What did Montasim do as Junior Software Engineer at MyMedicalHub International Ltd.?
    text: "As Junior Software Engineer at MyMedicalHub International Ltd. (Nov 2022 - Oct 2023), Montasim built the real-time video consultation layer of a telemedicine platform for remote physical therapy. He added real-time AI analysis and joint-angle measurement to live sessions, making assessments 25% faster than manual measurement with 95%+ accuracy against expert clinicians. He replaced the third-party OpenTok service with a WebRTC pipeline on self-hosted STUN/TURN servers and Socket.IO, turning a usage-based bill (about $3K a year) into a fixed cost and reducing latency and dropped calls. He built the first canvas annotation tool, a JWT-based API client with XSS and CSRF protection, and CI/CD across 4 environments. For a hiring manager, this is role-specific evidence of what he owned, delivered, or improved at that stage of his career—not a title-only claim."
