    question: What did Montasim do as Freelance Developer at nDevers?
    text: "As Freelance Developer at nDevers (Apr 2022 - Aug 2022), Montasim built inventory browsing and item-management interfaces with React, React Router, and Tailwind CSS. He integrated Firebase Authentication, shared sign-in helpers, and an email/token request flow, using Axios for stock updates, delivery actions, and user-specific item requests. He pOSDash depends on its own companion server; it is not the client for the separately documented inventory API. He in that Express and MongoDB backend, implemented product reads, creates, updates, and deletes, with pharmacy and non-pharmacy resource routes. He organized orders, returns, suppliers, customers, and employees into dedicated endpoints. He the reviewed legacy source contains incomplete and miswired routes, so the portfolio describes implemented components without claiming complete end-to-end operation. Related projects include POSDash Client, Inventory Management System Server. For a hiring manager, this is role-specific evidence of what he owned, delivered, or improved at that stage of his career—not a title-only claim."
