    supportingExcerpts[3]: "independent\nnDevers\nBuilt **inventory browsing and item-management interfaces** with React, React Router, and Tailwind CSS. Integrated **Firebase Authentication**, shared sign-in helpers, and an email/token request flow, using **Axios** for stock updates, delivery actions, and user-specific item requests. POSDash depends on its own companion server; it is not the client for the separately documented inventory API. In that **Express and MongoDB backend**, implemented product reads, creates, updates, and deletes,","true\nA legacy React inventory client with Firebase sign-in, item browsing, stock update and delivery controls, and user-specific item pages. Data workflows depend on a separate POSDash API.\nexperience-ndevers-freelance-developer\nfalse\n2022-04-29T16:39:44Z\n5533ac7ed486888f623f87681f057f602db19928\n2022-05-08T14:48:29Z\nfalse\nproject-warehouse-management-client\nnull\nJavaScript\nReact\nReact Router\nFirebase Authentication\nAxios\nTailwind CSS\nPOSDash Client\nlegacy-project\ninventory\nwebsite","true\nA legacy Express and MongoDB API organizing pharmacy and non-pharmacy products, orders, returns, customers, employees, and supplier records into resource routers.\nexperience-ndevers-freelance-developer\nfalse\n2022-07-20T15:29:19Z\na1e65bb3271ffe306f7af644fdcd1dc968fe1a3d\n2022-07-20T15:29:12Z\nfalse\nproject-inventory-management-system-server\nnull\nJavaScript\nNode.js\nExpress.js\nMongoDB\nInventory Management System Server\nlegacy-project\ninventory\napi"
