    question: What freelance or independent work has Montasim done?
    text: "Montasim documents freelance developer engagements with WaTheta, Infomax, TalendIT, nDevers. Infomax covers the API foundation for an MCQ learning platform; TalendIT covers school administration, admission-document handling, survey modeling, and web interfaces; nDevers covers inventory interfaces and backend resource operations. These engagements are listed separately from employment under Client work & Ventures."
    factIds[4]: "experience:experience-infomax-freelance-developer","experience:experience-watheta-freelance-developer","experience:experience-talendit-freelance-developer","experience:experience-ndevers-freelance-developer"
    supportingExcerpts[4]: "independent\nInfomax\nOrganized questions, exams, courses, enrolment, and results into **versioned Express modules** for an MCQ learning platform. Centralized **controller wrappers, response formatting, and error handling** to give new features a consistent API structure. Added Helmet security headers, request limits, timeouts, and rate limiting at the application boundary. Included **Nodemailer error notifications** and **Docker/PM2 deployment configuration**. The reviewed implementation establishes API","independent\nWaTheta\nContributed to the **CLM API messaging backend** with **WhatsApp, Messenger, and Instagram integrations**. Implemented inbound event handling and deduplication, **keyword-based automation**, and agent assignment by skill, department, and priority. Added **durable WhatsApp coexistence storage**, history synchronization, quoted replies, and **conversation SLA timers**. Implemented presence and typing events with **conversation access checks**, and added **unit and end-to-end test coverage**. The","independent\nTalendIT\nBuilt **Next.js and React school pages** for admissions, notices, routines, results, staff, and galleries, with responsive navigation, Swiper galleries, and a Google Maps integration. The frontend uses local sample content and an in-memory admin demonstration. In the school backend, implemented **Google Drive file handling** and stored admission-document identifiers and links in MongoDB. Separated controllers, persistence services, and **Joi input validation**. Built **Mongoose survey CRUD","independent\nnDevers\nBuilt **inventory browsing and item-management interfaces** with React, React Router, and Tailwind CSS. Integrated **Firebase Authentication**, shared sign-in helpers, and an email/token request flow, using **Axios** for stock updates, delivery actions, and user-specific item requests. POSDash depends on its own companion server; it is not the client for the separately documented inventory API. In that **Express and MongoDB backend**, implemented product reads, creates, updates, and deletes,"
