er’s perspective, what makes Montasim different is that he understands frontend development as a systems"
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:full-stack-fit"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: What supports hiring Montasim for a full-stack position?
    text: "Montasim's deepest evidence is frontend architecture, but his delivered work also covers PHP, Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, authentication, REST APIs, queues, cloud deployment, and CI/CD. PostCraft adds scheduled publishing, provider integration, persistent workflows, and multi-platform product logic, while his Codez role proves earlier client-driven PHP delivery. For Laravel teams, those backend foundations are transferable, but the current portfolio does not claim production Laravel experience; framework-specific depth should be assessed directly."
    factIds[6]: profile,"skills:skills-backend-apis","skills:skills-databases","experience:experience-codez-web-developer","project:project-postcraft","case-study:postcraft:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[6]: "I started as a junior engineer at MyMedicalHub International, and **4+ years** later I lead a team of **3 engineers** building a HIPAA-compliant platform that **1,000+ patients and clinicians** rely on. I am proudest that **99.9%** of their AI assessment sessions now finish without a crash, and that we got there while cutting our cloud bill by **70%**.\n\nHealthcare is where I work, but it is not the only thing I build. I have also shipped **education**, **fitness**, **customer messaging** and **AI creator**","Backend & APIs\nskills-backend-apis\nNode.js\nExpress.js\nSocket.io\nREST APIs\nBetter Auth\nNextAuth\nZod\nBullMQ\nInngest\nWeb Push\nResend\nStripe\nGoogle Drive API\nPython\nPHP\nNestJS\nMeta Graph API\nWhatsApp Cloud API\nMessenger API\nInstagram API\nMeta Conversions API\nGoogle Maps API\nFirebase Authentication\nJoi\nNodemailer","Databases & ORM\nskills-databases\nPostgreSQL\nMongoDB\nPrisma\nDrizzle ORM\nMongoose\nRedis\nSQLite\nPhpMyAdmin\nMariaDB\nMySQLi","employment\nCodez Info Tech.\n\nBuilt and maintained websites and web applications for **2 client projects** using **PHP, JavaScript and MySQL**. Turned client requirements into scoped features, and wrote and ran **test scenarios** before each release.\nexperience-codez-web-developer\nBadda, Dhaka, Bangladesh\nC\n/images/organizations/codez.png\nMay 2021 - Nov 2021\nWeb Developer\nPHP\nJavaScript\nMySQL\nHTML\nCSS","A social media manager that generates, scores, previews and schedules posts for LinkedIn, X and Facebook, using Gemini and stored brand guardrails.\n\ntrue\n2026-05-21T22:57:30Z\n664e1557c35eebde3bdb3a106447b4716e103b2c\n2026-05-26T16:29:25Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/PostCraft\nproject-postcraft\nassets/projects/postcraft.png\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app/favicon.ico?favicon.8ffa2b51.ico\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nMongoDB\nMongoose\nRedux Toolkit\nBetter Auth\nOpenRouter\nGemini API\nGroq","The workspace covers generation, scoring, editing, brand rules, and platform previews.\nWorkspace\nValidated domain workflows handle content, the library, accounts, and publishing.\nDomain services\nOpenRouter, Groq, Gemini, and ZhipuAI sit behind one switcher with model and key fallback.\nProvider layer\nMongoDB persists state, Inngest runs scheduled jobs, and social platform APIs receive the published posts.\nDelivery\nThe Next.js application keeps HTTP boundaries in route handlers, product logic in domain modules,"
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:ai-product-fit"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: Would Montasim fit a team building AI-enabled products?
    text: "Yes. He has production evidence across real-time healthcare AI, MediaPipe pose analysis, AI result visualization, Gemini-, Groq-, and OpenRouter-backed projects, and provider-aware product architecture. Crucially, his work emphasizes deterministic control, user trust, and provider boundaries rather than treating model output as automatically reliable."
