    supportingExcerpts[3]: "May 18, 2026\nMd. Tamim Tanvir, MBA\nworked with Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun but on different teams\nSenior Product Designer | Healthcare SaaS & Telemedicine | HIPAA-aware, WCAG accessible | 8+ yrs\nI had the opportunity to work closely with Montasim at MyMedicalHub International Ltd., where I led UX/UI design for our telemedicine and SaaS healthcare platforms while he led frontend engineering.\n\nFrom a designer’s perspective, what makes Montasim different is that he understands frontend development as a systems","June 5, 2025\nMd. Sazzad Hossain\nworked with Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun on the same team\nSoftware Engineer | Next.js 16 & React 19 Architecture | Full-Stack & Real-Time Systems (WebRTC, Socket.io) | AI & Cloud\nI highly recommend Montasim as an exceptional Frontend Software Engineer. I had the pleasure of collaborating closely with Montasim on the Telemedicine project at MyMedicalHub International Ltd., where we both made significant contributions to the front-end development.\n\nMontasim's expertise in frontend","May 26, 2025\nMd. Rifaet Ullah\nworked with Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun but on different teams\nSoftware Engineer | Django | AI | Machine Learning | Microservice\nMontasim is the rare engineer who effortlessly bridges the gap between research and production. At MyMedicalHUB International Ltd., he integrated our AI-driven analysis pipeline into a seamless user experience, building components that showcased annotated pictures and metric visualizations in real time. His passion for clean code and deep understanding of"
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:client-project-fit"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: Why might a client choose Montasim for a complex web product?
    text: "A client would get an engineer who can move from requirements and hidden constraints into architecture, implementation, testing, and reviewable outcomes. Montasim can demonstrate that process across SaaS, AI, browser extensions, data products, packages, and developer tools; his Codez role also directly records analyzing client needs, implementing the required functionality, and executing test scenarios. The best fit is a project that values clear technical boundaries and dependable delivery, not just rapid screen production."
    factIds[3]: "experience:experience-codez-web-developer","project:project-postcraft","case-study:postcraft:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "employment\nCodez Info Tech.\n\nBuilt and maintained websites and web applications for **2 client projects** using **PHP, JavaScript and MySQL**. Turned client requirements into scoped features, and wrote and ran **test scenarios** before each release.\nexperience-codez-web-developer\nBadda, Dhaka, Bangladesh\nC\n/images/organizations/codez.png\nMay 2021 - Nov 2021\nWeb Developer\nPHP\nJavaScript\nMySQL\nHTML\nCSS","A social media manager that generates, scores, previews and schedules posts for LinkedIn, X and Facebook, using Gemini and stored brand guardrails.\n\ntrue\n2026-05-21T22:57:30Z\n664e1557c35eebde3bdb3a106447b4716e103b2c\n2026-05-26T16:29:25Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/PostCraft\nproject-postcraft\nassets/projects/postcraft.png\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app/favicon.ico?favicon.8ffa2b51.ico\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nMongoDB\nMongoose\nRedux Toolkit\nBetter Auth\nOpenRouter\nGemini API\nGroq","One workspace now covers generation, comparison, refinement, preview, and delivery.\nProvider and key fallback reduce the workflow's dependency on a single AI endpoint.\nPublishing state is persisted for library and insights views instead of ending at generation.\nOperational limits remain explicit: publishing still depends on platform approval, scopes, account type, and API access."
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:startup-fit"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: What makes Montasim relevant to a fast-moving startup?
    text: "His portfolio shows breadth without losing delivery discipline: frontend and backend work, AI-provider integration, product experiments, CI/CD, cloud-cost ownership, and a broad independent-project record. The strongest evidence is his ability to turn ambiguous product constraints into explicit boundaries and testable outcomes."
    factIds[4]: profile,"experience:experience-mymedicalhub-software-engineer","case-study:thoughtline:architecture","case-study:postcraft:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[4]: "I started as a junior engineer at MyMedicalHub International, and **4+ years** later I lead a team of **3 engineers** building a HIPAA-compliant platform that **1,000+ patients and clinicians** rely on. I am proudest that **99.9%** of their AI assessment sessions now finish without a crash, and that we got there while cutting our cloud bill by **70%**.\n\nHealthcare is where I work, but it is not the only thing I build. I have also shipped **education**, **fitness**, **customer messaging** and **AI creator**","employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nOwned the biometric strength-assessment module end to end and led cloud cost and infrastructure work across **4 environments**. Cut cloud hosting cost **70%** (about **$10K a year**) by moving from self-managed VMs to **Azure App Service** with GitHub Actions CI/CD, and improved application performance **40%** to **Lighthouse 90+** by replacing 5 legacy UI libraries. Designed a **feature-flag system** and API-driven theming that serve **250+","LinkedIn content scripts extract the visible conversation, and a bounded manual input accepts pasted posts.\nPage integration\nReact side-panel workflows cover replies, ideas, refinement, history, settings, and onboarding.\nExtension interface\nTyped drafting and source-research ports use curated free OpenRouter models first, apply bounded provider timeouts, and fall back to Gemini and Groq.\nProvider boundary\nEncrypted browser storage, migrations, and backup and export features sit behind Manifest V3","One workspace now covers generation, comparison, refinement, preview, and delivery.\nProvider and key fallback reduce the workflow's dependency on a single AI endpoint.\nPublishing state is persisted for library and insights views instead of ending at generation.\nOperational limits remain explicit: publishing still depends on platform approval, scopes, account type, and API access."
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:enterprise-fit"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: What makes Montasim relevant to an enterprise platform?
    text: "His professional work includes multi-service healthcare SaaS, HIPAA-compliant SSO, multi-role access, OAuth, CSP, Azure migration, CI/CD, large-module refactoring, deterministic state, and formal PR review. Those records speak directly to security, maintainability, operational cost, and cross-team change."
