  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:ambiguity-handling"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: How does Montasim approach ambiguous engineering problems?
    text: "His case studies start by separating the visible feature from underlying constraints, then document boundaries, decisions, contribution, and outcomes. Thoughtline distinguishes page input, providers, credentials, and publish control; PostCraft separates request-time editing from durable scheduling. That is strong evidence of structured ambiguity reduction."
    factIds[3]: "case-study:thoughtline:problem","case-study:thoughtline:architecture","case-study:postcraft:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "Writing a useful LinkedIn reply or post requires understanding the visible conversation while keeping the author's own voice, intent, and control. The page is mutable third-party content, so passing it straight into a prompt would mix data, instructions, and potentially hostile text. An assistant that drafts well but cannot be trusted with page content and credentials is not useful.\nLinkedIn page content is untrusted and must be bounded before it enters any prompt.\nOpenRouter, Gemini, and Groq keys are all","LinkedIn content scripts extract the visible conversation, and a bounded manual input accepts pasted posts.\nPage integration\nReact side-panel workflows cover replies, ideas, refinement, history, settings, and onboarding.\nExtension interface\nTyped drafting and source-research ports use curated free OpenRouter models first, apply bounded provider timeouts, and fall back to Gemini and Groq.\nProvider boundary\nEncrypted browser storage, migrations, and backup and export features sit behind Manifest V3","The workspace covers generation, scoring, editing, brand rules, and platform previews.\nWorkspace\nValidated domain workflows handle content, the library, accounts, and publishing.\nDomain services\nOpenRouter, Groq, Gemini, and ZhipuAI sit behind one switcher with model and key fallback.\nProvider layer\nMongoDB persists state, Inngest runs scheduled jobs, and social platform APIs receive the published posts.\nDelivery\nThe Next.js application keeps HTTP boundaries in route handlers, product logic in domain modules,"
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:quality-discipline"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: What evidence shows Montasim values engineering quality?
    text: "The record includes automated testing, PR reviews, deterministic state, strict validation boundaries, performance measurement, and case studies that state limitations instead of hiding them. A QA colleague also describes clean, maintainable code, attention to detail, structured problem-solving, and consistent high-quality delivery."
