    factIds[4]: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer","project:project-postcraft","case-study:postcraft:outcomes","recommendation:1:tabbi-quadir"
    supportingExcerpts[4]: "employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nLead a team of **3 engineers** and own frontend architecture across **3 microservices** of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by **1,000+ patients and clinicians**. Replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic **finite-state-machine** engine, so **99.9%** of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with **60 FPS** MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. Built a **Konva.js**","A social media manager that generates, scores, previews and schedules posts for LinkedIn, X and Facebook, using Gemini and stored brand guardrails.\n\ntrue\n2026-05-21T22:57:30Z\n664e1557c35eebde3bdb3a106447b4716e103b2c\n2026-05-26T16:29:25Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/PostCraft\nproject-postcraft\nassets/projects/postcraft.png\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app/favicon.ico?favicon.8ffa2b51.ico\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nMongoDB\nMongoose\nRedux Toolkit\nBetter Auth\nOpenRouter\nGemini API\nGroq","One workspace now covers generation, comparison, refinement, preview, and delivery.\nProvider and key fallback reduce the workflow's dependency on a single AI endpoint.\nPublishing state is persisted for library and insights views instead of ending at generation.\nOperational limits remain explicit: publishing still depends on platform approval, scopes, account type, and API access.","May 25, 2025\nTabbi Quadir\nmanaged Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun directly\nProud contributor in accelerating digital transformation in Bangladesh\nI highly recommend Montasim Al Mamun as a skilled and dedicated software engineer. I had the pleasure of working with Montasim at MMHI.\n\nDuring our time together, I was consistently impressed by his technical abilities and commitment to delivering high-quality work. He demonstrated strong problem-solving skills and took a proactive approach to addressing challenges.\n\nMontasim"
