    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: Give a concise evidence-based hiring summary for Montasim.
    text: "Montasim is a Senior Software Engineer with two promotions, production healthcare SaaS depth, and measured results across reliability, real-time AI, frontend performance, cloud cost, and diagnosis workflows. He adds architecture ownership, mentoring, cross-functional credibility, and reviewable full-stack project work. Teams hiring for senior product engineering, frontend architecture, or AI-enabled SaaS should invite him to a role-specific technical conversation."
    factIds[5]: profile,"experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer","experience:experience-mymedicalhub-software-engineer","experience:experience-mymedicalhub-junior-software-engineer","recommendation:2:md-tamim-tanvir-mba"
    supportingExcerpts[5]: "I started as a junior engineer at MyMedicalHub International, and **4+ years** later I lead a team of **3 engineers** building a HIPAA-compliant platform that **1,000+ patients and clinicians** rely on. I am proudest that **99.9%** of their AI assessment sessions now finish without a crash, and that we got there while cutting our cloud bill by **70%**.\n\nHealthcare is where I work, but it is not the only thing I build. I have also shipped **education**, **fitness**, **customer messaging** and **AI creator**","employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nLead a team of **3 engineers** and own frontend architecture across **3 microservices** of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by **1,000+ patients and clinicians**. Replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic **finite-state-machine** engine, so **99.9%** of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with **60 FPS** MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. Built a **Konva.js**","employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nOwned the biometric strength-assessment module end to end and led cloud cost and infrastructure work across **4 environments**. Cut cloud hosting cost **70%** (about **$10K a year**) by moving from self-managed VMs to **Azure App Service** with GitHub Actions CI/CD, and improved application performance **40%** to **Lighthouse 90+** by replacing 5 legacy UI libraries. Designed a **feature-flag system** and API-driven theming that serve **250+","employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nBuilt the real-time video consultation layer of a telemedicine platform for remote physical therapy. Added real-time AI analysis and joint-angle measurement to live sessions, making assessments **25% faster** than manual measurement with **95%+ accuracy** against expert clinicians. Replaced the third-party OpenTok service with a **WebRTC** pipeline on self-hosted STUN/TURN servers and Socket.IO, turning a usage-based bill (about **$3K a year**)","May 18, 2026\nMd. Tamim Tanvir, MBA\nworked with Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun but on different teams\nSenior Product Designer | Healthcare SaaS & Telemedicine | HIPAA-aware, WCAG accessible | 8+ yrs\nI had the opportunity to work closely with Montasim at MyMedicalHub International Ltd., where I led UX/UI design for our telemedicine and SaaS healthcare platforms while he led frontend engineering.\n\nFrom a designer’s perspective, what makes Montasim different is that he understands frontend development as a systems"
