  - id: "technical-depth:frontend-architecture"
    category: technical-depth
    question: What is Montasim's strongest frontend-architecture example?
    text: "His healthcare biometric engine is the strongest professional example: Montasim replaced more than 40 unstable effect-driven interactions with a finite-state machine, creating deterministic transitions and reaching 99.9% reliability. The same role includes Redux Toolkit and a Presentational/Container refactor across 54+ chatbot modules."
    factIds[3]: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer",profile,"blog:from-useeffect-chaos-to-deterministic-systems"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nLead a team of **3 engineers** and own frontend architecture across **3 microservices** of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by **1,000+ patients and clinicians**. Replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic **finite-state-machine** engine, so **99.9%** of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with **60 FPS** MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. Built a **Konva.js**","I started as a junior engineer at MyMedicalHub International, and **4+ years** later I lead a team of **3 engineers** building a HIPAA-compliant platform that **1,000+ patients and clinicians** rely on. I am proudest that **99.9%** of their AI assessment sessions now finish without a crash, and that we got there while cutting our cloud bill by **70%**.\n\nHealthcare is where I work, but it is not the only thing I build. I have also shipped **education**, **fitness**, **customer messaging** and **AI creator**","Architecture\nI deleted 40+ useEffects and replaced them with a Finite State Machine. That was the best decision I made for our biometric assessment pipeline.\nfalse\nA deterministic state machine coordinating a real-time biometric assessment pipeline\n/images/blog/deterministic-systems.webp\nauthored\n2026-05-16\n3\nfrom-useeffect-chaos-to-deterministic-systems\nFrom useEffect Chaos to Deterministic Systems: Why I Rebuilt Our Biometric Pipeline with a Finite State Machine\nproduct"
  - id: "technical-depth:full-stack-evidence"
    category: technical-depth
    question: Which records demonstrate Montasim's full-stack range?
    text: "His role history includes React, Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL, JWT, WebRTC, Azure, Docker, and CI/CD. Project records add Next.js, MongoDB, Prisma, Drizzle, Better Auth, queues, scheduled jobs, email, APIs, and multiple AI providers, with case studies explaining how those parts are bounded."
    factIds[5]: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-junior-software-engineer","experience:experience-mymedicalhub-software-engineer","skills:skills-backend-apis","skills:skills-databases","project:project-postcraft"
    supportingExcerpts[5]: "employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nBuilt the real-time video consultation layer of a telemedicine platform for remote physical therapy. Added real-time AI analysis and joint-angle measurement to live sessions, making assessments **25% faster** than manual measurement with **95%+ accuracy** against expert clinicians. Replaced the third-party OpenTok service with a **WebRTC** pipeline on self-hosted STUN/TURN servers and Socket.IO, turning a usage-based bill (about **$3K a year**)","employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nOwned the biometric strength-assessment module end to end and led cloud cost and infrastructure work across **4 environments**. Cut cloud hosting cost **70%** (about **$10K a year**) by moving from self-managed VMs to **Azure App Service** with GitHub Actions CI/CD, and improved application performance **40%** to **Lighthouse 90+** by replacing 5 legacy UI libraries. Designed a **feature-flag system** and API-driven theming that serve **250+","Backend & APIs\nskills-backend-apis\nNode.js\nExpress.js\nSocket.io\nREST APIs\nBetter Auth\nNextAuth\nZod\nBullMQ\nInngest\nWeb Push\nResend\nStripe\nGoogle Drive API\nPython\nPHP\nNestJS\nMeta Graph API\nWhatsApp Cloud API\nMessenger API\nInstagram API\nMeta Conversions API\nGoogle Maps API\nFirebase Authentication\nJoi\nNodemailer","Databases & ORM\nskills-databases\nPostgreSQL\nMongoDB\nPrisma\nDrizzle ORM\nMongoose\nRedis\nSQLite\nPhpMyAdmin\nMariaDB\nMySQLi","A social media manager that generates, scores, previews and schedules posts for LinkedIn, X and Facebook, using Gemini and stored brand guardrails.\n\ntrue\n2026-05-21T22:57:30Z\n664e1557c35eebde3bdb3a106447b4716e103b2c\n2026-05-26T16:29:25Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/PostCraft\nproject-postcraft\nassets/projects/postcraft.png\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app/favicon.ico?favicon.8ffa2b51.ico\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nMongoDB\nMongoose\nRedux Toolkit\nBetter Auth\nOpenRouter\nGemini API\nGroq"
