    factIds[4]: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer","skills:skills-frontend","project:project-thoughtline","case-study:thoughtline:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[4]: "employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nLead a team of **3 engineers** and own frontend architecture across **3 microservices** of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by **1,000+ patients and clinicians**. Replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic **finite-state-machine** engine, so **99.9%** of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with **60 FPS** MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. Built a **Konva.js**","Frontend\nskills-frontend\nReact.js\nNext.js\nTypeScript\nJavaScript\nHTML5\nCSS\nTailwind CSS\nRedux.js\nTanStack Start\nTanStack Query\nReact Three Fiber\nThree.js\nDrei\nReact Three Rapier\nshadcn/ui\nRadix UI\nReact Hook Form\nReact Markdown\nCodeMirror 6\nnext-intl\nVite\nBootstrap\njQuery\nResponsive Web Design\nKonva.js\nReact Router\nSwiper\nAxios","User-controlled Chrome side-panel extension for drafting replies from pasted or selected LinkedIn posts, refining writing, and keeping every publish action manual.\n\nfalse\n2026-07-17T21:02:58Z\nb2085eead2f039535d2caf81c901d57c0028298a\n2026-07-17T20:56:56Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/Thoughtline\nproject-thoughtline\nassets/projects/thoughtline.png\nhttps://thoughtline.netlify.app\nhttps://thoughtline.netlify.app/brand/thoughtline-mark.svg\n\nhttps://github.com/montasim/Thoughtline/releases/latest\nWXT\nReact","LinkedIn content scripts extract the visible conversation, and a bounded manual input accepts pasted posts.\nPage integration\nReact side-panel workflows cover replies, ideas, refinement, history, settings, and onboarding.\nExtension interface\nTyped drafting and source-research ports use curated free OpenRouter models first, apply bounded provider timeouts, and fall back to Gemini and Groq.\nProvider boundary\nEncrypted browser storage, migrations, and backup and export features sit behind Manifest V3"
