    supportingExcerpts[5]: "employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nOwned the biometric strength-assessment module end to end and led cloud cost and infrastructure work across **4 environments**. Cut cloud hosting cost **70%** (about **$10K a year**) by moving from self-managed VMs to **Azure App Service** with GitHub Actions CI/CD, and improved application performance **40%** to **Lighthouse 90+** by replacing 5 legacy UI libraries. Designed a **feature-flag system** and API-driven theming that serve **250+","employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nBuilt the real-time video consultation layer of a telemedicine platform for remote physical therapy. Added real-time AI analysis and joint-angle measurement to live sessions, making assessments **25% faster** than manual measurement with **95%+ accuracy** against expert clinicians. Replaced the third-party OpenTok service with a **WebRTC** pipeline on self-hosted STUN/TURN servers and Socket.IO, turning a usage-based bill (about **$3K a year**)","Backend & APIs\nskills-backend-apis\nNode.js\nExpress.js\nSocket.io\nREST APIs\nBetter Auth\nNextAuth\nZod\nBullMQ\nInngest\nWeb Push\nResend\nStripe\nGoogle Drive API\nPython\nPHP\nNestJS\nMeta Graph API\nWhatsApp Cloud API\nMessenger API\nInstagram API\nMeta Conversions API\nGoogle Maps API\nFirebase Authentication\nJoi\nNodemailer","A social media manager that generates, scores, previews and schedules posts for LinkedIn, X and Facebook, using Gemini and stored brand guardrails.\n\ntrue\n2026-05-21T22:57:30Z\n664e1557c35eebde3bdb3a106447b4716e103b2c\n2026-05-26T16:29:25Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/PostCraft\nproject-postcraft\nassets/projects/postcraft.png\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app/favicon.ico?favicon.8ffa2b51.ico\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nMongoDB\nMongoose\nRedux Toolkit\nBetter Auth\nOpenRouter\nGemini API\nGroq","A theme-driven education website and content-management starter built with Next.js.\n\nfalse\n2026-07-27T17:41:53Z\nf0ea922b85f28025d1e3bf81d5a9b4ff413cda56\n2026-07-27T17:50:31Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/EduCanvas\nproject-educanvas\nassets/projects/educanvas.png\n\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nTailwind CSS\nMongoDB\nBetter Auth\nGoogle Drive API\nResend\nREST APIs\nRadix UI\nPlaywright\nSystem Design\nEduCanvas\ncontent-management\neducation\nnextjs\ntailwindcss\ntypescript\nwebsite-starter\ntemplate"
  - id: "technical-depth:data-modeling"
    category: technical-depth
    question: What examples show Montasim's data-modeling judgment?
    text: "His case studies model routine plans separately from outcomes, keep company evidence labeled by provenance, retain location-source provenance, and unify sharing lifecycles without erasing differences between links, text, and QR data. These examples prioritize semantics and trust over convenient but misleading schemas."
    factIds[4]: "case-study:routempo:architecture","case-study:b4joinacompany:architecture","case-study:bangladesh-location-registry:architecture","case-study:shrnkly:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[4]: "TanStack Start routes and React screens handle routine planning, daily execution, and review.\nInterface\nRoutine, session, and review services own timezone conversion and keep planned intent separate from recorded outcomes.\nDomain\nDrizzle repositories store durable behavioral records in Neon PostgreSQL, with Better Auth managing accounts.\nData and auth\nWeb Push and Google Calendar and Tasks adapters, plus scheduled summary endpoints, connect the planner to reminders and external calendars.\nIntegrations\nTanStack","Versioned records hold company, story, comment, and salary evidence.\nSource releases\nDeterministic rules handle identity matching, evidence labels, and question ranking.\nResearch layer\nNext.js serves research briefs, compare, and Ask, alongside a versioned REST API.\nProduct surfaces\nBetter Auth and MongoDB store private checkpoints pinned to evidence revisions.\nPrivate workspace\nVersioned source files feed a deterministic research layer. The web product and versioned API consume the same evidence model, while","Source and provenance manifests record where each dataset came from, what it covers, and its limitations.\nSource records\nSource data is normalized into geographic and facility records governed by JSON Schema.\nTransformation\nVersioned JSON, JSONL, compressed, and SQLite outputs are generated from the same model, with samples and documentation.\nRelease formats\nJavaScript scripts validate records against the schemas and produce deterministic release builds.\nValidation\nSource and provenance manifests describe where","Localized Next.js screens let users create short links, text shares, and QR codes.\nInterface\nServer actions and routes create records, resolve redirects, and check access rules on each request.\nDomain\nPrisma persists links, text shares, and account data to MongoDB.\nData and integrations\nAuthentication, input validation, and QR and browser-share adapters sit around the core creation and redirect flows.\nAuthentication and adapters\nA localized Next.js interface handles URL, text, and QR creation, while server actions"
  - id: "technical-depth:async-workflows"
    category: technical-depth
    question: How does Montasim design durable asynchronous workflows?
    text: "PostCraft separates interactive editing from durable scheduled delivery, persists reviewable job state, and avoids depending on an open browser tab or request. His release-oriented agent skills similarly model multi-system delivery as staged work with verification rather than pretending remote operations are atomic."
    factIds[2]: "case-study:postcraft:architecture","case-study:release-agent-skill:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[2]: "The workspace covers generation, scoring, editing, brand rules, and platform previews.\nWorkspace\nValidated domain workflows handle content, the library, accounts, and publishing.\nDomain services\nOpenRouter, Groq, Gemini, and ZhipuAI sit behind one switcher with model and key fallback.\nProvider layer\nMongoDB persists state, Inngest runs scheduled jobs, and social platform APIs receive the published posts.\nDelivery\nThe Next.js application keeps HTTP boundaries in route handlers, product logic in domain modules,","SKILL.md orchestrates the release stages the agent follows and the authorization each one needs.\nSkill workflow\nDeterministic references define the preflight checks and release gates that must pass before publication.\nAutomation\nAn npm installer, a package contract, and consumer-side tests confirm what users actually receive.\nVerification\nA SKILL.md file guides the agent through each release stage, backed by deterministic preflight and release-gate references. An npm installer and package contract, verified by"
  - id: "technical-depth:privacy-boundaries"
    category: technical-depth
    question: How does Montasim handle privacy and trust boundaries?
    text: "Examples include keeping tax-ID lookup client-side, treating LinkedIn page content as untrusted input, storing user-supplied provider keys locally in extension scope, labeling company-research evidence by source, and retaining provenance in public datasets. Each design limits what the system is allowed to infer or transmit."
    factIds[4]: "case-study:tin-audit-checker:architecture","case-study:thoughtline:architecture","case-study:b4joinacompany:architecture","case-study:bangladesh-location-registry:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[4]: "A responsive Next.js page accepts a TIN and shows the match state with its mapped details.\nLookup interface\nThe static JSON list is fetched once per session and kept in memory for every later search.\nSession dataset\nInput is stripped of formatting characters and compared by exact digits, with no TIN submission API behind it.\nClient-side matching\nA Next.js page fetches the static JSON dataset once per session and caches it in memory. Each search normalizes the input and runs an exact match in the browser, and there","LinkedIn content scripts extract the visible conversation, and a bounded manual input accepts pasted posts.\nPage integration\nReact side-panel workflows cover replies, ideas, refinement, history, settings, and onboarding.\nExtension interface\nTyped drafting and source-research ports use curated free OpenRouter models first, apply bounded provider timeouts, and fall back to Gemini and Groq.\nProvider boundary\nEncrypted browser storage, migrations, and backup and export features sit behind Manifest V3","Versioned records hold company, story, comment, and salary evidence.\nSource releases\nDeterministic rules handle identity matching, evidence labels, and question ranking.\nResearch layer\nNext.js serves research briefs, compare, and Ask, alongside a versioned REST API.\nProduct surfaces\nBetter Auth and MongoDB store private checkpoints pinned to evidence revisions.\nPrivate workspace\nVersioned source files feed a deterministic research layer. The web product and versioned API consume the same evidence model, while","Source and provenance manifests record where each dataset came from, what it covers, and its limitations.\nSource records\nSource data is normalized into geographic and facility records governed by JSON Schema.\nTransformation\nVersioned JSON, JSONL, compressed, and SQLite outputs are generated from the same model, with samples and documentation.\nRelease formats\nJavaScript scripts validate records against the schemas and produce deterministic release builds.\nValidation\nSource and provenance manifests describe where"
  - id: "technical-depth:scheduled-publishing"
    category: technical-depth
    question: How did Montasim architect scheduled social publishing?
    text: "PostCraft persists scheduling state and hands delivery to durable background execution instead of tying it to the request or browser session that created it. The case study also keeps generated variants, brand review, previews, and delivery status as explicit parts of the workflow."
    factIds[2]: "case-study:postcraft:architecture","case-study:postcraft:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[2]: "The workspace covers generation, scoring, editing, brand rules, and platform previews.\nWorkspace\nValidated domain workflows handle content, the library, accounts, and publishing.\nDomain services\nOpenRouter, Groq, Gemini, and ZhipuAI sit behind one switcher with model and key fallback.\nProvider layer\nMongoDB persists state, Inngest runs scheduled jobs, and social platform APIs receive the published posts.\nDelivery\nThe Next.js application keeps HTTP boundaries in route handlers, product logic in domain modules,","One workspace now covers generation, comparison, refinement, preview, and delivery.\nProvider and key fallback reduce the workflow's dependency on a single AI endpoint.\nPublishing state is persisted for library and insights views instead of ending at generation.\nOperational limits remain explicit: publishing still depends on platform approval, scopes, account type, and API access."
