    supportingExcerpts[5]: "The workspace covers generation, scoring, editing, brand rules, and platform previews.\nWorkspace\nValidated domain workflows handle content, the library, accounts, and publishing.\nDomain services\nOpenRouter, Groq, Gemini, and ZhipuAI sit behind one switcher with model and key fallback.\nProvider layer\nMongoDB persists state, Inngest runs scheduled jobs, and social platform APIs receive the published posts.\nDelivery\nThe Next.js application keeps HTTP boundaries in route handlers, product logic in domain modules,","LinkedIn content scripts extract the visible conversation, and a bounded manual input accepts pasted posts.\nPage integration\nReact side-panel workflows cover replies, ideas, refinement, history, settings, and onboarding.\nExtension interface\nTyped drafting and source-research ports use curated free OpenRouter models first, apply bounded provider timeouts, and fall back to Gemini and Groq.\nProvider boundary\nEncrypted browser storage, migrations, and backup and export features sit behind Manifest V3","Next.js routes host the accessible Atlas, which presents the professional history as a keyboard-friendly document.\nRoute shell and Atlas\nReact Three Fiber and Three.js render the explorable world, and Rapier handles physical interaction.\nScene runtime\nA deterministic journey compiler and generators produce route and world data from validated portfolio content.\nWorld data\nPlaywright, unit, and visual-baseline tests guard the compiler, interaction, and accessibility contracts, and the site ships as static","A navigation registry defines the searchable routes, labels, and keyboard discovery for every tool.\nTool registry\nFocused modules implement the formatters, generators, testers, inspectors, and references.\nFeature modules\nLocal transforms, preferences, input history, and reusable state stay in the browser.\nBrowser boundary\nNext.js APIs, Better Auth, PostgreSQL, Prisma, and target services handle the work that has to leave the browser.\nServer boundary\nA navigation registry acts as the catalog source of truth. Tool","Source and provenance manifests record where each dataset came from, what it covers, and its limitations.\nSource records\nSource data is normalized into geographic and facility records governed by JSON Schema.\nTransformation\nVersioned JSON, JSONL, compressed, and SQLite outputs are generated from the same model, with samples and documentation.\nRelease formats\nJavaScript scripts validate records against the schemas and produce deterministic release builds.\nValidation\nSource and provenance manifests describe where"
  - id: "technical-depth:deep-boundaries"
