  - id: "technical-depth:small-packages"
    category: technical-depth
    question: What does Montasim's package work reveal about API discipline?
    text: "His HTTP status, MIME type, content type, and client parser packages deliberately keep focused boundaries. Their case studies distinguish data from behavior, lookup from validation, and heuristic classification from certainty—useful evidence that he can make small APIs honest instead of expanding them without limits."
    factIds[4]: "case-study:http-status-lite:architecture","case-study:mime-types-lite:architecture","case-study:content-types-lite:architecture","case-study:client-parser:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[4]: "A committed IANA-derived registry generates the typed lookups, parsers, and status-class predicates.\nCore library\nConstants, predicates, and metadata ship as independently importable entry points alongside the complete main API.\nPackage builds\nAn interactive status reference consumes the local library, and automated workflows maintain the registry and handle releases.\nDocumentation app\nA committed snapshot of the IANA registry generates the typed library. Constants, predicates, and metadata are exposed as","A curated media-type registry backs pure functions for lookup and validation.\nCore library\nThe package is built with tsup into dual ESM and CommonJS formats with typed exports.\nPackage builds\nA workspace-linked TanStack Start app provides documentation and a playground that run against the local package.\nDocumentation app\nA curated media-type registry backs pure lookup and validation functions, which are built with tsup into a dual-format package with typed exports. A TanStack Start docs and playground app in the","Pure TypeScript functions parse, format, match, and validate media types, backed by tests.\nCore library\nThe tsup build produces dual ESM and CommonJS outputs with typed package exports.\nPackage builds\nA workspace-linked React documentation and playground app consumes the local package rather than a published release.\nDocumentation app\nThe core is a pure TypeScript library with its own tests, built into dual ESM and CommonJS outputs with typed exports. A React documentation and playground app in the same workspace","Pure parsing and normalization rules turn client strings and hints into a typed result model.\nCore library\nThe library ships as a zero-dependency package in both ESM and CommonJS formats.\nPackage builds\nA workspace-linked playground and docs app sits alongside a regression corpus of representative client strings.\nDocumentation app\nPure parsing and normalization rules produce a typed result model, packaged with zero dependencies in both ESM and CommonJS. A workspace-linked playground and documentation app runs the"
