  - id: "catalog-chronology-comparison:mymedicalhub-role-count"
    category: catalog-chronology-comparison
    question: How many MyMedicalHub roles document Montasim's progression?
    text: "3 successive MyMedicalHub records document his progression: Senior Software Engineer → Software Engineer → Junior Software Engineer. Their responsibilities expand from real-time AI and WebRTC to performance, cloud, security, and senior architecture leadership."
    factIds[3]: "experience:experience-mymedicalhub-senior-software-engineer","experience:experience-mymedicalhub-software-engineer","experience:experience-mymedicalhub-junior-software-engineer"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nLead a team of **3 engineers** and own frontend architecture across **3 microservices** of a HIPAA-compliant telemedicine and biometric-assessment platform used by **1,000+ patients and clinicians**. Replaced fragile React-hook state with a deterministic **finite-state-machine** engine, so **99.9%** of assessment sessions complete without a crash or freeze, with **60 FPS** MediaPipe pose estimation and real-time rep counting. Built a **Konva.js**","employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nOwned the biometric strength-assessment module end to end and led cloud cost and infrastructure work across **4 environments**. Cut cloud hosting cost **70%** (about **$10K a year**) by moving from self-managed VMs to **Azure App Service** with GitHub Actions CI/CD, and improved application performance **40%** to **Lighthouse 90+** by replacing 5 legacy UI libraries. Designed a **feature-flag system** and API-driven theming that serve **250+","employment\nMyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nBuilt the real-time video consultation layer of a telemedicine platform for remote physical therapy. Added real-time AI analysis and joint-angle measurement to live sessions, making assessments **25% faster** than manual measurement with **95%+ accuracy** against expert clinicians. Replaced the third-party OpenTok service with a **WebRTC** pipeline on self-hosted STUN/TURN servers and Socket.IO, turning a usage-based bill (about **$3K a year**)"
